<title>USA: Top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>Top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-05-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the U.S. box office for the May 16-18 weekend, according to studio estimates collected Sunday by Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc. Final results will be issued on Monday.</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>    1 (1) The Fifth Element ............. $11.6 million</p>
<p>    2 (2) Fathers' Day ..................  $6.4 million</p>
<p>    3 (3) Breakdown .....................  $6.1 million</p>
<p>    4 (4) Austin Powers:</p>
<p>	    International Man of Mystery ..  $5.6 million</p>
<p>    5 (5) Volcano .......................  $3.6 million</p>
<p>    6=(6) Liar Liar .....................  $3.0 million</p>
<p>    6=(*) Night Falls on Manhattan ......  $3.0 million</p>
<p>    8 (*) Sprung ........................  $2.5 million</p>
<p>    9 (7) Romy and Michele's High</p>
<p>	    School Reunion ................  $2.2 million</p>
<p>    10(8) Anaconda ......................  $2.1 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Last weekend's position in parenthesis. * denotes new release.</p>
<p>&quot;The Fifth Element&quot; was produced by Gaumont SA and released in the United States by Columbia Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp., which also released &quot;Anaconda.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Fathers' Day&quot; is released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc.. Time Warner's New Line Cinema released &quot;Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Breakdown&quot; and &quot;Night Falls on Manhattan&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Volcano&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Liar Liar&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
<p>&quot;Romy and Michele's High School Reunion&quot; is released by Walt Disney Co.</p>
<p>&quot;Sprung&quot; is released by Trimark Pictures.</p>
</text>
